I am getting off the bus.
It is evening time.
I am walking towards my house.
There are many people on the street.
They are all going home.
I need milk and bread.
There is a small shop on the way.
I buy things from here every day.
I am stopping at the shop.
I say to the shopkeeper, "Hello brother."
The shopkeeper says, "Hello madam."
I say, "Brother, please give one packet of milk and one bread."
The shopkeeper is giving me the items.
I ask, "Brother, how many rupees?"
He says, "Fifty rupees."
I am giving him the money.
I am putting the items in my bag.
Now I am walking again.
My house is very close.
